    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2362" root="برك" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرْكَةٌ</span></b> , (S, K,) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرَكَةٌ</span></b> , (Msb,) <i>A certain
aquatic bird, white,</i> (S, Msb, K,) <i>and small:</i>
(K:) [the former applied in Barbary, in the
present day, to <i>a duck:</i>] pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرَكٌ</span> (S, Msb, K) and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرْكَانٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِرْكَانٌ</span> and [pl. of pauc.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبْرَاكٌ</span>; (K;)
or, in the opinion of ISd, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ابراك</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بركان</span> are
pls. of the pl. [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرَكٌ</span>]. (TA.)

